SRC/whetstone -- the Whetstone benchmark, as built for OS-9/68000=================================================================whetstone.c is the file from the Microware OS-9 archive's benchmarksdirectory, a C translation of Curnow and Wichmann's 1976 Algolbenchmark already adapted for OSK.  It is unchanged; ORIG holds thesame file.  Built with the recipe `whetstone', -qm, so it needs no cio.It times itself with clock(), which counts the process's own ticks.It runs 20 iterations of the benchmark's module mix and prints theseconds taken and the rating: Whetstone instructions per second.